    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.23.6</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:43:23 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22306</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.23.6</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Squeak cloud now lives in Settings › Account. If this Mac isn't connected yet, press Connect… there; Settings › Cloud is gone.</li><li>Fixes Settings saying you were signed in while still asking you to sign in.</li><li>Model names read the same everywhere, like Opus 5.5 · 1M and GPT 6.1 Sol, instead of raw ids.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.5</h4><ul><li>Squeak now runs the cloud for you: sign in to Squeak and your phone, browser and Cliq can reach this Mac. There's no Firebase or Catalyst to set up anymore.</li><li>A Mac on its own Firebase, Squeak's old shared server or its own Catalyst relay keeps working, and moves to Squeak's cloud when you sign in; paired devices follow.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.4</h4><ul><li>A long chat no longer opens to a blank transcript: it keeps scrolling to the newest message until it is on screen.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
